# ==============================================================================
# CAV MULTI-STATE ANALYSIS: REPORTING TABLES AND FIGURES
# ==============================================================================
# Produces SAP Tables 3, 4, 6 and 7, model-derived tables, a publication-ready
# Sahlgrenska prevalence figure, and one Excel workbook for SAS reporting.
#
# State coding assumed:
#   1 = CAV 0, 2 = CAV 1, 3 = CAV >=2, 4 = Death, 99 = alive/CAV unknown.
#
# Assumes the final long data already contain the annual age-update rows and
# the artificial cut-point row where required.
#
# No event-count or event-rate columns are produced for the multi-state model.
# ============================================================================

